<<say "Serena Waves" "I… I don’t mean to be rude… But please don't come any closer." "frightened">>
<<stage "Her voice is tiny, soft, and fragile like fine china. Saying the wrong thing will likely make her swim away.">>
<<timed 2s t8n>>
<<choices>>
<<reply "I'm not going to hurt you." A1 Serena Waves Talk 2a 5>>
<<reply "She's scared of her own shadow, this one..." A1 Serena Waves Talk 2b -5>>
<<reply "Okay okay, I'll keep my distance." A1 Serena Waves Talk 4 5>>
<</choices>>
<</timed>>

:: A1 Serena Waves Talk 2a [dialogue act1 char-Serena Waves]
<<stage "The woman's tail swings in and out of view at a nervous pace for a few seconds. She then slowly pokes her head out enough to look at you with her right eye for a brief moment before darting back behind the building. You can see her tail tense up in obvious fear.">>
<<say "Serena Waves" "So... so scary!" "fearful whisper">>
<<stage "It is obvious to you now that this merfolk is frightened by your appearance. Perhaps a change in subject is in order?">>
<<choices>>
<<reply "You know, I saw this huge scaly whale on my way down here. What do you know about it?" A1 Serena Waves Talk 3a 10>>
<<reply "Am I still scary when I do... this?" A1 Serena Waves Talk 3b 15>>
<<reply "Sorry... I'll take my leave then." A1 Serena Waves Talk 4>>
<</choices>>

:: A1 Serena Waves Talk 2b [dialogue act1 char-Serena Waves]
<<stage "Your words only make her whimper a bit more loudly, perhaps in agreement. A different approach is required if you want her to open up.">>
<<choices>>
<<reply "I just remembered, there was a giant whale with scales I saw during my descent." A1 Serena Waves Talk 3a 10>>
<<reply "Me and my big mouth..." A1 Serena Waves Talk 4>>
<</choices>>

:: A1 Serena Waves Talk 3a [dialogue act1 char-Serena Waves]
<<stage "Her tail instantly starts to swing excitedly. Within a second, she swims up to you quick as a flash, revealing a beaming smile and sparkling eyes, her fear forgotten.">>
<<say "Serena Waves" "The Scaleback Whale! I know of that creature! It is one of the largest whales to ever been seen by Merfolk. Its scales on its back vary in color. Some whales have blue scales, others have green scales. Why, I've even seen one with scales that have multiple colors, which is extremely rare!" "deeply excited">>
<<stage "She immediately becomes silent and her eyes grow wide with shock as she realizes that she had just talked to you. Blushing profusely, she swims away without saying another word, leaving you dumbfounded.>>
<<choices>>
<<reply "Well, at least I got her to come out of her shell... or scales." A1 Serena Waves Talk 4>>
<</choices>>

:: A1 Serena Waves Talk 3b [dialogue act1 char-Serena Waves]
<<stage "You decide to peform a simplistic dance in an attempt to amuse the merfolk. Your slow movements and the stomping of your boots make the dance seem quite silly. Just as you had hoped for. The woman peaks out from behind the building again, intrigued by your dance. She can't help but let out an amused giggle in spite of her fear. Slowly, her giggling turns into laughter while she floats fully into view.">>
<<say "Serena Waves" "You're so funny! Just like Eelis!" "In between her laughs">>
<<stage "Her laughter slows down and stops after a few seconds. Now calm and not so frightened, she speaks to you with a grateful tone.">>
<<say "Serena Waves" "I'm glad you're not so scary.">>
<<stage "She swims into the dark of the alleyway and out of sight.">>
<<choices>>
<<reply "Nothing distracts someone from their fears better than comedy." A1 Serena Waves Talk 4>>
<</choices>>

